          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "Control-room view of Kuma monitors, with sampled status history and rolling availability. Group monitors are separate from individual monitors. Prometheus does not expose the parent-child hierarchy, so nested groups cannot be reconstructed. Monitor type and ID filters apply throughout. Missing history is never painted green.\n\nGreen, amber and red indicate explicit status. Blue is quantitative emphasis. N/A means missing or unsupported data, never healthy zero.",
